doug@robo.austin.ibm.com (Doug Bagley) writes:

>I would like to see all the patches rolled into a new version sometime
>soon.  I believe this has been mentioned before.  What does the
>community think?

I'd like to see some more changes before all these patches become a new
version. First, I'd like to see alignment become more fluid. As someone
else suggested, alignment would be more fun if you could chhose it as an
option. I'm also in the camp that thinks good and evil should be separate
from chaotic and lawful. Perhaps some of the alignment inconsistencies
should be worked out before a NEW version is put out. Also, can we do
anything about those doors? I'm getting used to them, but it would be a
lot better if there were at least some way to distinguish closed from open
doors just by looking at the screen. I like the fact that we can "chat"
with monsters in this version. :) Could we have that feature expanded? How
about having certain intelligent creatures capable of a conversation? If
the P.C. said the wrong thing, it could start a fight. If the P.C. said
something particularly clever (or if they are really charismatic :) they
could stop a fight or steal some gold or (gasp!) seduce a monster... Also,
it seems a bit silly to have people die of overeating. Why not have P.C.'s
vomit if they eat too much, or pass out, or get slow, or lose charisma
points or something? Maybe you could die of overeating if the gods are mad
at you and you eat too much. Of course, I wish the game was a little
easier to win, but I guess "the experts" like it hard. That's alright...
maybe I'll win someday. :)


